<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Heydar Aliyev</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1923–2003</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Heydar Aliyev was a KGB officer who led the Communist Party of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> SSR from 1969 to 1982 and then became a member of the Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/politburo">Politburo</a>. He returned to power in independent Azerbaijan in 1993 and as president agreed the 1994 ceasefire in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-nagorno-karabakh-war">First Karabakh War</a> and the 'Contract of the Century' with Western oil companies. He built a strong presidential system, passed in 2003 to his son Ilham.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/heydar-aliyev.jpg" alt="Heydar Aliyev" width="320" height="387" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Press Service of the President of the Republic of Azerbaijan · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heydar_Aliyev_(crop).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
